First, I can't help but notice that you picked a tag for yourself that
truly suits you.

Monsters can be generated peaceful.  If it is a monster with the
ability or will to dig, it will...randomly.  If you identify the
monster ( ';' command ) it will say if it is peaceful (or tame).  If
you are not confused or hallucinating, you will be asked if you REALLY
want to attack the peaceful monster.  Big hint:  if Nethack asks if you
really want to do something, there is probably a very good reason why
you should think twice about it.  (The real problem is the vast number
of things that you can do which give you no warning.)

However, your pet doesn't make such fine distinctions.  If Fluffy
thinks she can take the dwarf, she will.  You can either let this
process proceed, or intervene in some way.  It's up to you.

Your next problem is this:  think about it, dude; if someone were
throwing pears at you, would you like it?  And if you had a pickaxe in
your possession, what would you do with it?

Your penultimate problem is this:  if a monster is generated peaceful,
it stays 'peaceful' in the game's model.  Even if it changes it's mind
and takes a swing at you.

Your final problem is this: it seems you have acquired the 'aggravate'
intrinsic.  After the game asks DYWYPI?, it will ask about the monsters
killed and your intrinsics.  Check this to make sure after you're done.



